---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {countries} from '../../lib/resume';
export function getStaticPaths(){return countries.map(c=>({params:{country:c.slug},props:{country:c}}))}
const {country:c}=Astro.props;
const content:Record<string,{intro:string,focus:string[],example:string,source?:string,label?:string}>={
 US:{intro:'For a US job application, build a focused resume around the evidence that matters to the role. A complete career history is useful as a master profile; the version you submit should be selective.',focus:['Choose Letter paper as a starting point, and follow any format instructions from the employer.','Use familiar headings such as Experience, Education and Skills. Write out unfamiliar abbreviations.','Describe your contribution with specific examples. Include a measurable result only when you can verify it.','Use a straightforward single-column layout when applying through an online portal.'],example:'Before: Responsible for customer support.\nAfter: Resolved customer inquiries, documented recurring issues and helped update the team’s support guide.',source:'https://cloudfront.careeronestop.org/JobSearch/Resumes/ResumeGuide/formatting.aspx',label:'CareerOneStop resume formatting guidance'},
 GB:{intro:'A UK CV should help an employer quickly connect your experience to their vacancy. Start with a focused introduction, then choose an order that puts your most relevant evidence first.',focus:['Leave out age, date of birth, marital status and nationality, in line with National Careers Service guidance.','Use a brief personal profile supported by evidence elsewhere in the CV. Avoid broad claims without examples.','List relevant employment and education clearly. For a first role, give projects and volunteering meaningful space.','Use A4 as your starting paper size and check the employer’s requested format.'],example:'Before: Excellent team player.\nAfter: Coordinated weekly handovers with a four-person team and kept shared project notes up to date.',source:'https://nationalcareers.service.gov.uk/careers-advice/cv-sections',label:'National Careers Service: How to write a CV'},
 AE:{intro:'Employers in the UAE cover many industries and working environments. There is no single CV layout that suits every application. Use the vacancy as your starting point and make your relevant experience easy to find.',focus:['State your location clearly. If relocation is relevant, explain your plans accurately rather than implying you are already based locally.','Highlight relevant sector experience and the tools or qualifications named in the vacancy, where you actually have them.','List languages with an honest description of proficiency. Do not assume that every role needs the same languages.','Include eligibility or availability details only if useful or requested. This builder does not collect passport numbers or other sensitive identifiers.'],example:'For an accounting role, put verified qualifications, reporting responsibilities and the accounting systems you use near the top. For a design role, prioritize a portfolio link and relevant project outcomes.'},
 SA:{intro:'For applications in Saudi Arabia, tailor the document to the employer’s stated requirements. A concise, clearly organized CV can show relevant experience without making assumptions about every company’s preferences.',focus:['Check the language requested in the job advert. GlobalCV currently provides an English-first editing and export experience.','For technical or regulated roles, include relevant verified qualifications and current certifications. Do not claim eligibility you have not established.','Make project responsibilities, tools and outcomes specific enough to discuss in an interview.','Keep dates consistent and provide reliable contact information. Follow employer instructions on supporting documents.'],example:'For an engineering application, describe the type of project, your responsibilities, the tools you used and your contribution. Mention licenses only if they are current and relevant.'},
 PK:{intro:'Whether you are applying for your first job in Pakistan or moving into a more senior role, use your CV to show relevant evidence. You do not need to fill space with unrelated information.',focus:['For a first role, place education, internships and projects before a short or empty employment history.','Describe what you personally contributed to a class or team project. Separate your work from the overall team result.','List relevant tools and skills that you can demonstrate. Avoid adding every skill mentioned in the vacancy.','Use professional contact details and a clear location. Avoid adding a CNIC number or other sensitive identifiers to a general-purpose CV.'],example:'For a graduate developer, describe one project: the problem it solves, the technology used and what you built. Link to a public repository only if it is ready for employers to review.'}
};
const guide=content[c.code];
---
<Layout title={`${c.name} Resume & CV Guide`} active="guides" description={`Practical guidance for a resume or CV for ${c.name}. Create a free, clear application document and download it without an account.`}><main id="main" class="content-page article"><a href="/guides/">← All career guides</a><div style="margin-top:30px" class="eyebrow">APPLYING IN {c.name.toUpperCase()}</div><h1>A clear CV for your next opportunity in {c.name}.</h1><p class="lead">{guide.intro}</p><h2>What to focus on</h2><ul>{guide.focus.map(x=><li>{x}</li>)}</ul><h2>Make the evidence specific</h2><p class="preserve-lines">{guide.example}</p><h2>Before you send it</h2><ol><li>Read the vacancy again and check that your strongest relevant evidence is easy to find.</li><li>Confirm your dates, contact details, links and spelling.</li><li>Download the PDF, check each page, and make sure text can be selected.</li><li>Submit the requested file type. Employer instructions take priority over general advice.</li></ol><div class="article-note"><strong>Guidance, not a universal country rule.</strong><p style="margin-bottom:0">These are practical starting points. Requirements vary by employer, role and industry. Choosing a country in GlobalCV changes guidance and paper size; it does not certify eligibility or guarantee selection.</p></div>{guide.source&&<p>Reference: <a href={guide.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{guide.label}</a>.</p>}<a class="button primary" href={`/builder/?country=${c.code}`}>Build your {c.short} resume →</a></main></Layout>
